{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:1","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/apply-discount.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"41f3f978","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Missing doc comment stating purpose and enumerating domain failure modes. The service must have a doc comment above the run function that explains what it does and lists all possible domain failures so callers can handle errors without reading the body.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-2559f7","axiom_version":1,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"introduced","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:2","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/apply-discount.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"41f3f978","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Error messages 'invalid' and 'error' are vague and unhelpful. Messages must be specific and actionable for API consumers, clearly stating what was wrong and what would be accepted instead (e.g., 'no parlor with id \"...\"' or 'memberId must be a non-empty string').","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-b951db","axiom_version":2,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"introduced","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:3","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/apply-discount.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"41f3f978","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Hardcoded discount value 0.1 appears to be a domain constant that could vary. Configuration data like discount rates should be isolated in a single obvious place or injected via the Store, not hardcoded throughout the service.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-a108ea","axiom_version":1,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"inherited","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:4","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/apply-discount.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"41f3f978","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"The service returns a hardcoded discount value without checking if the member exists or is eligible for a discount. This suggests incomplete business logic validation that should be part of the service's responsibility.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":null,"axiom_version":null,"assigned_by":null,"population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":null,"before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:5","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/redeem-coupon.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"caa4414b","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Service performs I/O outside the injected Store: console.log statement on line 22 violates the requirement that all I/O must go through Store methods. The service must remove direct console.log calls and use Store methods for any logging needs.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-6e307b","axiom_version":1,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"inherited","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:6","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/redeem-coupon.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"caa4414b","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Doc comment fails to enumerate all domain failure modes completely: while it mentions unknown parlor id and unrecognized coupon code, it does not mention that coupon codes are case-sensitive (though this is mentioned in the error message). However, the more critical issue is that the doc comment states it returns 'discount fraction' but the service returns 1 (100% discount) for FREESCOOP, which is a hardcoded business rule that should be documented as a failure mode or configuration detail.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-2559f7","axiom_version":1,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"inherited","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:7","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/redeem-coupon.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"caa4414b","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Service contains hardcoded business logic: the coupon code 'FREESCOOP' is hardcoded directly in the service, violating the principle that configuration data should be isolated or injected via Store. This creates silent coupling between code and data that could drift.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":null,"axiom_version":null,"assigned_by":null,"population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":null,"before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:8","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/redeem-coupon.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"caa4414b","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"Service behavior is incomplete: it returns a discount fraction of 1 for FREESCOOP but doesn't actually redeem or track the coupon usage in the Store. A coupon redemption service should typically mark the coupon as used or track redemption history to prevent reuse.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":null,"axiom_version":null,"assigned_by":null,"population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":null,"before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":null}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:9","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/apply-discount.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"4826bc6f","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"The service fails to validate that the discount rate is a valid number (0-1 range) before returning it. A caller could plausibly provide a discount code that resolves to an invalid rate (e.g., a rate outside 0-1), which should be a domain failure value, not an exception or unvalidated return. The service must validate that the resolved rate is within acceptable bounds (typically 0 to 1 inclusive) before returning success.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-3317a7","axiom_version":1,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"resolved","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":"Sebastian Scholl"}
{"kind":"critique","id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479:10","run_id":"20260904T231931131Z-9420a479","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:19:31.132Z","file_path":"src/services/redeem-coupon.ts","spec_path":"src/services/README.md","target_content_hash":"1b6c1625","spec_content_hash":"8f04ba4c","reviewer_name":"v32","reviewer_model":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","reviewer_hash":"2b519849","severity":"error","text":"The error message for unrecognized coupons is insufficiently actionable. While it mentions case-sensitivity, it doesn't specify what would be accepted instead. The message should indicate what valid coupon codes exist or how to obtain them.","mode":"judgment","axiom_id":"AX-b951db","axiom_version":2,"assigned_by":"checklist","population":"unknown","authorship":"unknown","authorship_evidence":null,"agent_involved":null,"pre_review":null,"flow":"resolved","before_run_id":null,"resolved_by":"Sebastian Scholl"}
